1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,138
You pump more blood than you have.

2
00:00:02,318 --> 00:00:04,977
One London doctor proved it with a sum.

3
00:00:05,197 --> 00:00:07,818
Say the heart holds two ounces.

4
00:00:07,946 --> 00:00:10,858
Each beat, an eighth of that goes out.

5
00:00:11,018 --> 00:00:14,538
In half an hour, it beats more than a thousand times.

6
00:00:14,634 --> 00:00:17,178
That's more blood than your whole body holds.

7
00:00:17,338 --> 00:00:19,658
Food could never make that much.

8
00:00:19,818 --> 00:00:23,498
So it's the same blood, going round and round.
